§ `Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019, Part 2 -- fees`

§§ `The nouns`

DECLARE `The Tribunal fee` IS ONE OF
    `filing an initiating process (item 1)`
    `filing a cross-claim (item 2)`
    `filing a notice of motion (item 3)`
    `the first directions hearing (item 4)`
    `issuing a subpoena for production (item 5)`
    `issuing a subpoena to give evidence (item 6)`
    `issuing a subpoena for production and to give evidence (item 7)`
    `the registrar receiving a document produced under a notice to produce (item 8)`
    `sealed or certified copies of a judgment or order (item 13)`
    `a duplicate recording of sound-recorded evidence, per disc (item 14)`
    `requesting production of documents held by another court (item 15)`
    `another service the registrar approves a fee for (item 17)`

DECLARE `The financial year` IS ONE OF
    `before 1 July 2022`
    `2022-23`
    `2023-24`
    `2024-25`
    `1 July 2025 or later`

DECLARE `The kind of fee for postponement` IS ONE OF
    `the filing fee for my initiating process or cross-claim`
    `another fee in the proceedings`

DECLARE `The judgment so far` IS ONE OF
    `no judgment yet`
    `judgment for me, with costs and damages`
    `judgment for me, with damages but no costs`
    `judgment for me, with costs but no damages or only nominal damages`
    `judgment for me, with neither costs nor more than nominal damages`
    `judgment against me`

DECLARE `What happens to my fee` IS ONE OF
    `postponed until judgment is given (cl 6(1) or 7(1)); the registrar must not refuse to file your documents meanwhile`
    `not to be taken at all, or remitted if it was taken (cl 6(2) or 7(2))`
    `payable now: judgment has been given in your favour with costs and damages`
    `the text is unclear where only one of costs and damages is awarded (fork F9)`
    `payable in the usual way when the document is filed or the service rendered (cl 10(1)), unless the registrar postpones, waives or remits it (cl 10(2))`

DECLARE `Who pays the first directions hearing fee` IS ONE OF
    `no fee: the hearing only gives effect to a settlement (cl 9(4))`
    `the parties, in the proportions the Tribunal ordered (cl 9(1)(a))`
    `the cross-claimant, or the first cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(b))`
    `you, the claimant, not any cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(c)); your solicitor is jointly and severally liable with you (cl 9(2))`
    `you, the claimant, not any cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(c))`

§§ `Sch 1 -- the fee unit and the fees`

-- Sch 1 Part 1, Column 2 (standard fee, in fee units), the flat items.
GIVEN fee IS A `The Tribunal fee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard fee in fee units for` fee MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `filing an initiating process (item 1)` THEN 2.16
    WHEN `filing a cross-claim (item 2)` THEN 2.16
    WHEN `filing a notice of motion (item 3)` THEN 2.23
    WHEN `the first directions hearing (item 4)` THEN 8.61
    WHEN `issuing a subpoena for production (item 5)` THEN 0.87
    WHEN `issuing a subpoena to give evidence (item 6)` THEN 0.42
    WHEN `issuing a subpoena for production and to give evidence (item 7)` THEN 0.87
    WHEN `the registrar receiving a document produced under a notice to produce (item 8)` THEN 0.87
    WHEN `sealed or certified copies of a judgment or order (item 13)` THEN 0.75
    WHEN `a duplicate recording of sound-recorded evidence, per disc (item 14)` THEN 0.56
    WHEN `requesting production of documents held by another court (item 15)` THEN 0.64
    WHEN `another service the registrar approves a fee for (item 17)` THEN 0.45

-- Sch 1 Part 2 cl 2(1)(a) "in the financial year 2022-2023--$103.05"; the Editorial note under cl 2: "2023-24 $110.93",
-- "2024-25 $115.59". The cl 2(1)(b) formula is lost from the deposited text (finding 2).
GIVEN year IS A `The financial year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fee unit in dollars for` year MEANS
    CONSIDER year
    WHEN `2022-23` THEN JUST 103.05
    WHEN `2023-24` THEN JUST 110.93
    WHEN `2024-25` THEN JUST 115.59
    WHEN `before 1 July 2022` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (this version of Schedule 1 starts at 2022-23; an earlier version is not deposited)
    WHEN `1 July 2025 or later` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the CPI formula is lost from the deposited text and the Editorial note stops at 2024-25)

@export What is the Dust Diseases Tribunal's fee for this, in dollars, for me as an individual in this financial year (cl 4, Sch 1)?
GIVEN fee IS A `The Tribunal fee` @desc Which fee: filing an initiating process, a cross-claim or a notice of motion; the first directions hearing; issuing a subpoena; receiving a produced document; sealed copies; a duplicate recording; requesting another court's documents; another approved service
      year IS A `The financial year` @desc The financial year (1 July to 30 June) in which the fee is taken
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is this Tribunal fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fee unit in dollars for` year
    WHEN JUST unit THEN JUST (`rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` (`the standard fee in fee units for` fee TIMES unit))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (no fee unit for that year in the deposited text)

§§ `cl 6, 7 -- postponed and waived fees`

-- cl 6(1) the filing fee for an initiating process (or cross-claim) of a pro bono party "is to be postponed until judgment
-- has been given"; (2) "The fee is not to be taken at all, or if taken must be remitted, if ... (a) judgment is against
-- that party, or (b) judgment is in favour of that party, but costs and damages are not awarded (or only nominal damages
-- are awarded) in the party's favour." (4) a pro bono party is one represented under the Law Society's or the Bar
-- Association's pro bono scheme, with a solicitor's or barrister's written certificate to the registrar. cl 7 does the
-- same for any fee payable by a pensioner party (holding a Commonwealth health concession card) or a legally assisted
-- party (assisted through a community legal service).
@export Is my Dust Diseases Tribunal fee postponed until judgment, or not taken at all, because I am a pro bono, pensioner or legally assisted party (cl 6, 7)?
GIVEN `the kind of fee` IS A `The kind of fee for postponement` @desc Whether the fee is the filing fee for your initiating process or cross-claim, or another fee in the proceedings
      `I am represented under a Law Society or Bar Association pro bono scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are represented under the pro bono scheme of the Law Society of NSW or the NSW Bar Association
      `my lawyer certified that in writing to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your solicitor (or barrister) certified in writing to the registrar that you are so represented
      `I hold a Commonwealth health concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a card issued by the Commonwealth that entitles you to Commonwealth health concessions (for example a pensioner concession card)
      `I am legally assisted by a community legal service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving legal assistance through a community legal service
      judgment IS A `The judgment so far` @desc Whether judgment has been given and, if so, for or against you and with what costs and damages
GIVETH A `What happens to my fee`
`Is my fee postponed or waived` MEANS
    IF `cl 7 applies` OR `cl 6 applies`
    THEN CONSIDER judgment
         WHEN `no judgment yet` THEN `postponed until judgment is given (cl 6(1) or 7(1)); the registrar must not refuse to file your documents meanwhile`
         WHEN `judgment against me` THEN `not to be taken at all, or remitted if it was taken (cl 6(2) or 7(2))`
         WHEN `judgment for me, with neither costs nor more than nominal damages` THEN `not to be taken at all, or remitted if it was taken (cl 6(2) or 7(2))`
         WHEN `judgment for me, with costs and damages` THEN `payable now: judgment has been given in your favour with costs and damages`
         OTHERWISE `the text is unclear where only one of costs and damages is awarded (fork F9)`
    ELSE `payable in the usual way when the document is filed or the service rendered (cl 10(1)), unless the registrar postpones, waives or remits it (cl 10(2))`
    WHERE
        `cl 7 applies` MEANS `I hold a Commonwealth health concession card` OR `I am legally assisted by a community legal service`
        `cl 6 applies` MEANS
                `I am represented under a Law Society or Bar Association pro bono scheme`
            AND `my lawyer certified that in writing to the registrar`
            AND (CONSIDER `the kind of fee`
                 WHEN `the filing fee for my initiating process or cross-claim` THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `cl 9 -- the first directions hearing fee`

-- cl 9(1) the fee is payable "(a) if the Tribunal makes an order as to the payment of the fee--by the parties in the
-- proportions so ordered, (b) if the hearing involves a cross-claim or more than one cross-claim only--by the
-- cross-claimant or first cross-claimant in any cross-claim, (c) in any other case--by the claimant (and not by any
-- cross-claimant)." (2) a party and the solicitor carrying on the proceedings are jointly and severally liable. (4) not
-- payable for a hearing to give effect to a settlement.
@export Who pays the first directions hearing fee in my Dust Diseases Tribunal claim (cl 9(1), (2), (4))?
GIVEN `the hearing only gives effect to a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing is only for the Tribunal to make orders giving effect to the parties' settlement
      `the Tribunal ordered how the fee is shared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has made an order about who pays the fee
      `the hearing involves only cross-claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing involves only a cross-claim or cross-claims (not your own claim)
      `a solicitor carries on my proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a solicitor (or other person) is carrying on the proceedings for you
GIVETH A `Who pays the first directions hearing fee`
`Who pays the first directions hearing fee` MEANS
    IF `the hearing only gives effect to a settlement`
    THEN `no fee: the hearing only gives effect to a settlement (cl 9(4))`
    ELSE IF `the Tribunal ordered how the fee is shared`
         THEN `the parties, in the proportions the Tribunal ordered (cl 9(1)(a))`
         ELSE IF `the hearing involves only cross-claims`
              THEN `the cross-claimant, or the first cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(b))`
              ELSE IF `a solicitor carries on my proceedings`
                   THEN `you, the claimant, not any cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(c)); your solicitor is jointly and severally liable with you (cl 9(2))`
                   ELSE `you, the claimant, not any cross-claimant (cl 9(1)(c))`

-- cl 9(3) the fee "becomes payable-- (a) immediately after a date is allocated for the first directions hearing in the
-- Tribunal, as referred to in clause 67, or (b) immediately after a date is allocated for the first directions hearing
-- ... for a claim determined to be urgent ..., or (c) when the Tribunal or registrar notifies the parties in writing of
-- the Tribunal's intention to allocate a date for a first directions hearing ..., whichever occurs first."
@export On what day does the first directions hearing fee become payable in my Dust Diseases Tribunal claim (cl 9(3))?
GIVEN `a hearing date has been allocated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a date has been allocated for the first directions hearing (after the claims resolution process, or for an urgent claim)
      `the day the hearing date was allocated` IS A DATE @desc The day that date was allocated (any date if none)
      `the parties were notified of an intention to allocate a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal or registrar notified the parties in writing that it intends to allocate a date for a first directions hearing
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that written notice (any date if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When does the first directions hearing fee become payable` MEANS
    IF `a hearing date has been allocated` AND `the parties were notified of an intention to allocate a date`
    THEN IF DATE_SERIAL `the day of that notice` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the day the hearing date was allocated`
         THEN JUST `the day of that notice`
         ELSE JUST `the day the hearing date was allocated`
    ELSE IF `a hearing date has been allocated`
         THEN JUST `the day the hearing date was allocated`
         ELSE IF `the parties were notified of an intention to allocate a date`
              THEN JUST `the day of that notice`
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (none of the three events has happened: not yet payable)
